{"database" "math" "lineage" "01a12a15-3e0a-75a1-9dac-f8b8c5d5c3f1" "basis" 4908 "entities" [{:db/id 17592186110593 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186110494 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id 17592186110593 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34f4b65e-b93a-51e8-b943-b3b53d47fffb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Solutions to Exponential Equations Using Logarithms"}] :question/id #uuid "7c937587-dc81-5ee9-aa66-a509a87433e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4067" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $2^{x+1}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take $\\log_2$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x+1} & =3 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡({2}^{x+1}) & ={log}_{2}⁡(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b \\left( b^c \\right) = c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx+1 = \\log_2 \\left( 3 \\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & ={log}_{2}⁡(3) \\\\ x & ={log}_{2}⁡(3)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x= \\log_2 \\left( 3 \\right) - 1.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34f4b65e-b93a-51e8-b943-b3b53d47fffb" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186111048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id 17592186110593 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34f4b65e-b93a-51e8-b943-b3b53d47fffb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Exact Solutions to Exponential Equations Using Logarithms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96f390d2-efc8-5d3d-85fc-6ccafa7aae81" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\log_{3} (2) + 3" :db/id 17592186108046} {:answer/id #uuid "dd912690-9404-550b-aba4-589ca100a0a7" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\log_{3} (6) - 2" :db/id 17592186108047} {:answer/id #uuid "faffe04e-ba23-54cf-b9ac-8fad1be7c554" :answer/type {:db/id 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = \\log_{3} (4)" :db/id 1759